nts, taking Black from +2.2 to -29.6, the biggest loss of the game. The engine wanted B4 here. After this the 20k's moves at B2, B4 and D1 each lost less than a point, and Black never got back into it."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script (the `act` wrapper, `inspect`, `analyze`, `place`, and the replay/SGF code) only parses boards, computes chains and liberties, and evaluates the one placement the player named; the replay just re-plays the actual moves to verify them. Nothing loops over candidate moves or plays a sequence forward, and the rest is file reading and note writing.", "stop": false}}